1
00:00:47,777 --> 00:00:51,072
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:56,244 --> 00:00:58,872
Sangwon Police Major Crimes Unit.
Mr. Park Hae-kang?

3
00:00:59,539 --> 00:01:01,332
You're under arrest

4
00:01:01,416 --> 00:01:03,042
for embezzlement and breach of trust.

5
00:01:03,126 --> 00:01:06,754
Due to the risk of flight,
we're arresting you without a warrant.

6
00:01:06,838 --> 00:01:09,090
You have the right to retain an attorney,

7
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:11,259
to present your defense,
and to remain silent.

8
00:01:11,759 --> 00:01:14,095
Anything you say can
and will be used against you--

9
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:15,054
Let's go.

10
00:01:20,310 --> 00:01:21,311
There he is!

11
00:01:31,362 --> 00:01:32,447
Just a moment.

12
00:01:34,198 --> 00:01:35,617
THE TRUTH BEHIND THE TRUE VALUE STATE SCAM

13
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:37,493
HUMAN SCUM DESERVE MERCILESS PUNISHMENT

14
00:01:40,747 --> 00:01:41,831
Let's keep moving.

15
00:01:44,292 --> 00:01:46,085
I supported you!

16
00:01:46,169 --> 00:01:48,212
I feel so betrayed!

17
00:01:57,805 --> 00:01:58,640
Wait!

18
00:02:04,896 --> 00:02:06,522
Guys! Don't!

19
00:02:07,190 --> 00:02:09,651
How can you do this when you're a mom?

20
00:02:09,734 --> 00:02:10,777
Mr. Park!

21
00:02:12,362 --> 00:02:13,488
Take care of our family.

22
00:02:20,995 --> 00:02:22,372
Boss!

23
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:26,709
Boss!

24
00:02:42,183 --> 00:02:47,563
THE APARTMENT JOB

25
00:02:56,781 --> 00:02:59,200
You came up with great lines, Mr. Kim.

26
00:02:59,283 --> 00:03:00,368
Good job.

27
00:03:00,451 --> 00:03:02,161
I like the photos too.

28
00:03:02,245 --> 00:03:04,831
It's been a while
since I got such an adrenaline rush.

29
00:03:06,582 --> 00:03:08,292
Should I put this on my living room wall?

30
00:03:08,376 --> 00:03:11,546
I can look at it whenever I'm sad.
It'll help with my depression.

31
00:03:11,629 --> 00:03:13,715
We stuck about 1,000 posters
around the complex

32
00:03:13,798 --> 00:03:15,508
and placed them in all the mailboxes.

33
00:03:15,591 --> 00:03:19,637
By tomorrow,
everyone will know about Park Hae-kang.

34
00:03:20,513 --> 00:03:21,848
Right.

35
00:03:21,931 --> 00:03:24,350
This is the scary thing
about an apartment complex.

36
00:03:24,434 --> 00:03:28,021
Once you're branded as a fraud,
you can't step outside your door.

37
00:03:28,104 --> 00:03:30,523
All 9,800 households will be watching him.

38
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:33,526
How would he endure that?

39
00:03:35,403 --> 00:03:36,988
-Mr. Kim.
-Yes, sir.

40
00:03:37,071 --> 00:03:38,781
Forget about eating healthy today.

41
00:03:39,365 --> 00:03:42,285
How about some spicy rice cakes?
I want them very spicy.

42
00:03:44,787 --> 00:03:46,539
So spicy

43
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:49,375
that it'll bring tears to your eyes.

44
00:03:58,801 --> 00:04:01,054
I know your situation,
but give us the ledger.

45
00:04:01,137 --> 00:04:02,221
We need to save our boss.

46
00:04:02,972 --> 00:04:05,308
Ha-ri, give them the ledger.

47
00:04:06,225 --> 00:04:07,602
It was an emergency arrest.

48
00:04:07,685 --> 00:04:10,396
They have to release him
if they can't get a warrant in 48 hours.

49
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:13,649
But who knows what will happen to him
within the 48 hours?

50
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:15,902
There's no point in bringing the ledger.

51
00:04:15,985 --> 00:04:17,445
Lee Chung-won's name

52
00:04:17,528 --> 00:04:19,530
isn't even written in there.

53
00:04:21,991 --> 00:04:25,411
The names written there
were President Seo and Mr. Choi.

54
00:04:25,495 --> 00:04:28,748
There's no connection
to Lee Chung-won whatsoever.

55
00:04:32,543 --> 00:04:36,089
Back then, I didn't know
that Lee Chung-won was behind it.

56
00:04:36,172 --> 00:04:39,008
But I've met him in person,
so if I testify…

57
00:04:39,092 --> 00:04:40,218
Don't you get it?

58
00:04:40,301 --> 00:04:41,969
Lee Chung-won planned all this.

59
00:04:42,053 --> 00:04:44,555
If we bring the ledger,
it will only help him.

60
00:04:44,639 --> 00:04:48,101
You mean he'll pin the blame
on Mr. Choi, President Seo,

61
00:04:48,184 --> 00:04:51,229
and Ms. Kang Ha-jeong
once he gets his hands on the ledger?

62
00:04:54,023 --> 00:04:57,819
I recorded everything in a way
that it'd be really easy for him

63
00:04:58,653 --> 00:05:00,446
to shift all the blame to us.

64
00:05:01,656 --> 00:05:03,241
Well, I…

65
00:05:05,118 --> 00:05:06,077
Then…

66
00:05:06,828 --> 00:05:08,371
what about our boss?

67
00:05:11,207 --> 00:05:12,917
Lee Chung-won's trying to pressure us.

68
00:05:13,584 --> 00:05:15,253
He wants our fake family to scatter

69
00:05:15,336 --> 00:05:17,964
and disappear from this apartment complex.

70
00:05:18,047 --> 00:05:19,632
What Lee Chung-won wanted

71
00:05:19,715 --> 00:05:21,634
was the image
of Park Hae-kang getting arrested

72
00:05:21,717 --> 00:05:23,219
so it would rattle the residents.

73
00:05:23,302 --> 00:05:25,888
So what? We just do nothing?

74
00:05:26,472 --> 00:05:28,141
He'll be released in 48 hours.

75
00:05:28,224 --> 00:05:29,559
Forty-eight…

76
00:05:30,184 --> 00:05:31,352
Also,

77
00:05:31,436 --> 00:05:34,730
didn't you hear Mr. Park telling us
to take care of the family?

78
00:05:34,814 --> 00:05:36,441
We should be sticking together.

79
00:05:36,524 --> 00:05:38,651
Stick together and do what?

80
00:05:39,444 --> 00:05:41,779
We have to stay right here, as a family.

81
00:05:42,989 --> 00:05:46,284
If we all flee because of this,
we'll really become frauds.

82
00:05:46,367 --> 00:05:48,578
It's true we're a fake family,

83
00:05:48,661 --> 00:05:50,163
but we didn't embezzle anything.

84
00:05:55,084 --> 00:05:57,336
So if we run away, we become frauds,

85
00:05:58,588 --> 00:06:01,174
and if we stay, we remain a family?

86
00:06:02,884 --> 00:06:05,261
So we should stay here
and be a real family

87
00:06:06,012 --> 00:06:09,140
so Mr. Park can return and fight, right?

88
00:06:10,308 --> 00:06:11,309
Yes.

89
00:06:11,893 --> 00:06:14,854
All 9,800 households are watching us.

90
00:06:30,286 --> 00:06:32,288
The system clearly says
there's 17.8 billion.

91
00:06:32,371 --> 00:06:34,081
How is the account empty?

92
00:06:34,165 --> 00:06:36,918
We had no idea that the account
didn't match the system.

93
00:06:37,001 --> 00:06:38,961
We only found out today.

94
00:06:40,546 --> 00:06:44,383
You practically gave away the key
to someone who made a fake family

95
00:06:44,467 --> 00:06:47,053
to embezzle
the long-term repair reserve fund!

96
00:06:47,136 --> 00:06:49,430
And we had no idea!

97
00:06:49,513 --> 00:06:53,226
We were stupidly praising him
and calling him President Park!

98
00:06:53,309 --> 00:06:54,310
We're sorry.

99
00:06:54,393 --> 00:06:56,479
We really had no idea.

100
00:06:56,562 --> 00:06:59,774
President Park managed the seal
and account himself.

101
00:06:59,857 --> 00:07:01,776
How is that an excuse?

102
00:07:01,859 --> 00:07:05,279
But we won't even be able to pay
the cleaning company next month.

103
00:07:06,239 --> 00:07:08,199
To keep the complex running,

104
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:11,535
we'll have to collect a special assessment

105
00:07:11,619 --> 00:07:13,663
of about 1.82 million won per household.

106
00:07:13,746 --> 00:07:15,498
What? 1.82 million?

107
00:07:15,581 --> 00:07:17,667
Are you kidding me?

108
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:20,670
Why should I pay for the money
that Park Hae-kang pocketed?

109
00:07:20,753 --> 00:07:22,964
I'm never going to pay for that!

110
00:07:23,047 --> 00:07:26,217
That 1.82 million won
isn't the problem right now!

111
00:07:27,009 --> 00:07:29,470
The kindergarten's closed down
due to shoddy construction,

112
00:07:29,554 --> 00:07:32,473
the maintenance fees are out of control,
and the reserve fund is gone.

113
00:07:32,557 --> 00:07:34,350
If word spreads about this,

114
00:07:34,433 --> 00:07:36,519
our property value will plummet!

115
00:07:36,602 --> 00:07:39,272
Our apartment complex
could really go under overnight.

116
00:07:39,355 --> 00:07:42,024
We should freeze the assets
of that scammer family

117
00:07:42,108 --> 00:07:44,986
and cut off
all their electricity and water!

118
00:07:47,947 --> 00:07:50,533
Do you really think
we got scammed by them?

119
00:07:50,616 --> 00:07:51,826
I can't believe it either.

120
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:55,037
The problem is his face.

121
00:07:55,788 --> 00:07:57,623
How could a fraud look like that?

122
00:07:57,707 --> 00:07:59,375
His acting was way too good.

123
00:07:59,458 --> 00:08:01,002
Forget his face.

124
00:08:01,085 --> 00:08:02,795
He's a fraud

125
00:08:02,878 --> 00:08:04,380
who embezzled all our money.

126
00:08:04,463 --> 00:08:05,464
Hey.

127
00:08:06,882 --> 00:08:08,968
You have no loyalty at all.

128
00:08:09,051 --> 00:08:12,221
You shouldn't treat him like this.

129
00:08:12,305 --> 00:08:16,642
Did you forget who stepped up
and helped with the kindergarten issue?

130
00:08:16,726 --> 00:08:18,019
That's not all.

131
00:08:18,102 --> 00:08:21,188
Remember what he did about
the deliveries and the heating bills?

132
00:08:22,106 --> 00:08:23,232
Then what about this?

133
00:08:23,316 --> 00:08:25,067
There's a photo of him at the bank.

134
00:08:25,151 --> 00:08:27,486
We're not sure what to believe anymore.

135
00:08:28,279 --> 00:08:31,032
It's simple. You should trust the money.

136
00:08:31,115 --> 00:08:33,451
That 17.8 billion isn't some pocket money.

137
00:08:33,534 --> 00:08:36,203
If he really took all that,
why would he remain here

138
00:08:36,287 --> 00:08:37,997
and work so hard?

139
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,457
Does that make any sense?

140
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:41,417
If he really embezzled 17.8 billion,

141
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,127
he would've changed his identity

142
00:08:43,210 --> 00:08:46,088
and already fled the country,
don't you think?

143
00:08:46,672 --> 00:08:47,548
You're right.

144
00:08:48,591 --> 00:08:52,011
Before we think about whether
Park Hae-kang's a fraud or not,

145
00:08:52,637 --> 00:08:55,181
we should think about finding
our 17.8 billion won.

146
00:08:55,264 --> 00:08:59,268
You young mothers,
use your brains, will you?

147
00:09:02,396 --> 00:09:03,814
This is tough.

148
00:09:04,732 --> 00:09:05,941
My goodness.

149
00:09:07,568 --> 00:09:09,487
TENANTS' COUNCIL
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN

150
00:09:12,948 --> 00:09:17,370
How can this be the face of someone
who took 17.8 billion won?

151
00:09:17,453 --> 00:09:21,248
He looks like
he's the one who got robbed blind.

152
00:09:34,845 --> 00:09:36,222
EXPOSING PARK HAE-KANG'S CORRUPTION

153
00:09:36,847 --> 00:09:37,807
I swear

154
00:09:39,475 --> 00:09:43,437
that I have not taken so much
as a single penny in illicit gains.

155
00:09:44,397 --> 00:09:46,065
I promise to cooperate

156
00:09:46,565 --> 00:09:49,777
with any investigations.

157
00:09:51,362 --> 00:09:53,614
Lastly, I sincerely apologize
to all the residents

158
00:09:54,573 --> 00:09:56,158
of True Value.

159
00:10:05,543 --> 00:10:07,628
Cut! Okay!

160
00:10:09,046 --> 00:10:10,297
Good job.

161
00:10:11,757 --> 00:10:12,758
Mr. Choi,

162
00:10:13,718 --> 00:10:15,636
you saw President Seo last time, right?

163
00:10:22,601 --> 00:10:25,062
A disappearance

164
00:10:25,146 --> 00:10:27,022
is neat and convenient.

165
00:10:27,982 --> 00:10:30,609
No body, no evidence.

166
00:10:31,485 --> 00:10:33,404
It only leaves hope

167
00:10:33,988 --> 00:10:36,282
for their family.

168
00:10:36,866 --> 00:10:40,286
You know that's the state
President Seo is in, don't you?

169
00:10:41,704 --> 00:10:43,330
Yes.

170
00:10:44,915 --> 00:10:48,043
I'll do anything you ask, sir.

171
00:10:51,255 --> 00:10:52,631
I'm counting on you.

172
00:10:58,721 --> 00:10:59,638
I need to live.

173
00:11:00,973 --> 00:11:02,391
I have to survive first.

174
00:11:22,411 --> 00:11:23,704
Mr. Choi.

175
00:11:23,787 --> 00:11:24,788
What?

176
00:11:27,124 --> 00:11:28,375
Where are you going?

177
00:11:29,585 --> 00:11:30,711
I have urgent business…

178
00:11:30,794 --> 00:11:32,421
By any chance,

179
00:11:32,505 --> 00:11:33,881
are you running away?

180
00:11:35,257 --> 00:11:37,551
Running away? No, I need to go…

181
00:11:38,093 --> 00:11:38,969
Let me talk to you.

182
00:11:39,053 --> 00:11:40,429
Is it true

183
00:11:40,513 --> 00:11:43,057
that President Park
embezzled the reserve fund?

184
00:11:43,807 --> 00:11:46,060
He didn't.
It was President Seo, wasn't it?

185
00:11:46,143 --> 00:11:48,604
You and President Seo
embezzled the fund, didn't you?

186
00:11:48,687 --> 00:11:49,647
Didn't you?

187
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:52,107
-Let go of me.
-Don't you dare.

188
00:11:52,191 --> 00:11:53,192
What's with you?

189
00:11:55,110 --> 00:11:56,820
Get him!

190
00:11:56,904 --> 00:11:58,072
Catch that thief!

191
00:12:01,909 --> 00:12:03,494
Taxi!

192
00:12:03,577 --> 00:12:04,703
Taxi! Stop!

193
00:12:04,787 --> 00:12:05,829
Taxi!

194
00:12:09,375 --> 00:12:10,960
Sir, go! Just go!

195
00:12:12,378 --> 00:12:13,837
Where should I take you,

196
00:12:14,547 --> 00:12:15,464
sir?

197
00:12:22,179 --> 00:12:24,473
Hide, hide

198
00:12:24,557 --> 00:12:25,516
What?

199
00:12:25,599 --> 00:12:27,309
Hey, it's nice to see you!

200
00:12:27,393 --> 00:12:29,186
Take this. Good to see you.

201
00:12:29,895 --> 00:12:31,397
Get that jerk!

202
00:12:32,189 --> 00:12:33,315
Got you!

203
00:12:34,066 --> 00:12:36,569
It's so nice to see you! How are you here?

204
00:12:36,652 --> 00:12:37,611
Who's that?

205
00:12:41,615 --> 00:12:43,325
SEOUL SANGWON POLICE STATION

206
00:13:07,099 --> 00:13:09,351
I put a lot of effort into making this.

207
00:13:09,935 --> 00:13:10,853
Do you like it?

208
00:13:12,479 --> 00:13:14,398
You should've put more effort

209
00:13:15,149 --> 00:13:18,110
into building the kindergarten.

210
00:13:20,571 --> 00:13:23,991
You've really got nerves of steel.

211
00:13:24,950 --> 00:13:26,035
Here's a quiz.

212
00:13:26,785 --> 00:13:29,872
There's no evidence anywhere
that you actually embezzled

213
00:13:29,955 --> 00:13:31,040
the 17.8 billion won.

214
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:33,334
So why did I lock you up in here?

215
00:13:34,418 --> 00:13:36,295
This is boring.

216
00:13:37,254 --> 00:13:39,923
Number one, to screw you over.

217
00:13:40,758 --> 00:13:43,761
Number two,
to give you a warning not to act up.

218
00:13:44,762 --> 00:13:45,846
Guess the answer.

219
00:13:48,724 --> 00:13:49,975
Number three.

220
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:52,019
You're right.

221
00:13:54,396 --> 00:13:55,481
You really are smart.

222
00:13:55,981 --> 00:13:59,485
Shifting the narrative
and damaging your credibility.

223
00:13:59,568 --> 00:14:03,864
People won't be so sure about you

224
00:14:04,657 --> 00:14:06,617
embezzling the 17.8 billion won,

225
00:14:07,201 --> 00:14:10,329
but they can immediately accept
you making a fake family.

226
00:14:11,205 --> 00:14:14,792
They'll easily believe
that you were a fraud who faked it

227
00:14:14,875 --> 00:14:18,087
to embezzle 17.8 billion won.

228
00:14:19,046 --> 00:14:21,882
I'm actually curious.

229
00:14:22,466 --> 00:14:23,717
Did you really think

230
00:14:24,385 --> 00:14:28,764
exposing that shoddy construction
would achieve some great justice?

231
00:14:29,682 --> 00:14:33,060
Is there any construction in Korea
that isn't shoddy?

232
00:14:33,894 --> 00:14:36,480
Penthouses in Gangnam worth billions,

233
00:14:36,563 --> 00:14:39,358
nameless apartment complexes
in the middle of nowhere…

234
00:14:39,441 --> 00:14:41,694
They're actually all the same.

235
00:14:44,029 --> 00:14:45,447
Is shoddy construction

236
00:14:46,323 --> 00:14:47,741
something to brag about?

237
00:14:48,325 --> 00:14:50,244
In the face of shoddy construction,

238
00:14:50,327 --> 00:14:52,579
everyone is equal.

239
00:14:52,663 --> 00:14:54,790
There's no rich or poor.

240
00:14:58,544 --> 00:15:00,254
That's how everyone lives.

241
00:15:00,337 --> 00:15:02,214
That's the norm in this business.

242
00:15:02,297 --> 00:15:03,173
Commissioner.

243
00:15:04,591 --> 00:15:06,885
The grounds for arresting Park
without a warrant

244
00:15:06,969 --> 00:15:08,595
are weak.

245
00:15:10,597 --> 00:15:12,433
We did go a little too far.

246
00:15:18,105 --> 00:15:21,525
Look at that arrogant piece of shit.

247
00:15:21,608 --> 00:15:23,444
He thinks the law and the police

248
00:15:23,527 --> 00:15:25,696
are all below him right now.

249
00:15:27,364 --> 00:15:30,159
Mr. Lee says he does have a plan,

250
00:15:30,242 --> 00:15:33,037
but judging by the way he talks,

251
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:35,497
he's a ticking time bomb.

252
00:15:36,165 --> 00:15:38,042
If we get hit by the fallout,

253
00:15:38,751 --> 00:15:40,169
we're done for.

254
00:15:42,838 --> 00:15:44,256
Taesan's been under fire lately

255
00:15:44,339 --> 00:15:46,717
because of the shoddy
kindergarten construction.

256
00:15:48,218 --> 00:15:49,970
Dig into that more properly.

257
00:15:50,554 --> 00:15:52,848
We can't keep wiping his ass forever.

258
00:15:53,766 --> 00:15:57,311
I need to have some leverage over him too.

259
00:16:00,230 --> 00:16:01,231
Yes, sir.

260
00:16:03,358 --> 00:16:06,445
I was going to get you released
for getting the right answer,

261
00:16:07,988 --> 00:16:08,989
but I don't want to.

262
00:16:09,073 --> 00:16:11,700
You can take the full 48 hours here

263
00:16:11,784 --> 00:16:14,036
to reflect on yourself.

264
00:16:18,999 --> 00:16:22,669
I'll tell them to add extra meat
to your soup.

265
00:16:22,753 --> 00:16:24,046
Enjoy your meal.

266
00:16:29,676 --> 00:16:31,303
Your photos look great.

267
00:16:45,692 --> 00:16:48,445
Sir, the facility manager
didn't get on the plane.

268
00:16:50,697 --> 00:16:53,367
Mr. Kim, stay on your toes.

269
00:16:53,450 --> 00:16:55,828
I'm sorry, sir.
I'll get my men to find him.

270
00:16:58,372 --> 00:17:00,916
I wonder where Mr. Choi is hiding.

271
00:17:02,417 --> 00:17:03,877
He'd better not cause trouble

272
00:17:03,961 --> 00:17:06,130
if he doesn't want
to end up as fertilizer.

273
00:17:09,091 --> 00:17:12,970
When will a sunny day come for me?

274
00:17:13,554 --> 00:17:15,389
-When will…
-Look! Over there!

275
00:17:15,472 --> 00:17:17,850
-Isn't that President Park's father?
-It is.

276
00:17:19,893 --> 00:17:21,353
Hey, you fraud!

277
00:17:21,436 --> 00:17:24,148
Darn it. I'm so popular,
the ladies won't leave me alone.

278
00:17:24,231 --> 00:17:26,275
-Hello.
-Hello.

279
00:17:26,358 --> 00:17:28,026
Wait, just a moment.

280
00:17:28,110 --> 00:17:28,986
Close it!

281
00:17:29,069 --> 00:17:30,362
Hurry!

282
00:17:30,445 --> 00:17:31,864
Don't let her in.

283
00:17:31,947 --> 00:17:33,365
Use the next one!

284
00:17:33,448 --> 00:17:36,076
Let's all go up together.

285
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:38,162
-How obnoxious.
-There's plenty of space.

286
00:17:40,706 --> 00:17:42,291
They stuck them here too?

287
00:17:42,374 --> 00:17:44,293
Everyone already saw these.

288
00:17:49,131 --> 00:17:50,924
YOU THIEVES
DON'T PARK IN OUR PARKING LOT

289
00:17:52,885 --> 00:17:54,344
LEAVE, YOU FAKE FAMILY

290
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:04,605
Let's go.

291
00:18:07,191 --> 00:18:09,359
EVEN THIEVES NEED A PLACE TO PARK!

292
00:18:09,443 --> 00:18:10,861
THANKS FOR THE MESSAGE

293
00:18:11,612 --> 00:18:12,529
Did it hurt?

294
00:18:14,573 --> 00:18:18,076
You know, in life,
there are rites of passage.

295
00:18:19,578 --> 00:18:23,040
Everyone goes through them at some point.

296
00:18:23,123 --> 00:18:25,000
-A trip to the dentist is one of those.
-Mom.

297
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:27,419
Can we ride a slide before we go home?

298
00:18:28,629 --> 00:18:29,546
A slide?

299
00:18:31,089 --> 00:18:32,216
Deal.

300
00:18:35,219 --> 00:18:36,887
-Ha-yul.
-Let's go.

301
00:18:36,970 --> 00:18:38,055
Let's go home.

302
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:40,766
-Come on. Let's go.
-Come here.

303
00:18:41,850 --> 00:18:43,352
-I want to play some more.
-No.

304
00:18:45,562 --> 00:18:46,980
Mom.

305
00:18:48,273 --> 00:18:49,983
Do they hate us

306
00:18:50,651 --> 00:18:53,487
because we're a fake family?

307
00:18:56,990 --> 00:18:57,824
Gyeong-buk.

308
00:18:58,784 --> 00:19:00,869
What do you think is fake?

309
00:19:02,746 --> 00:19:05,123
Is it real if you're related by blood?

310
00:19:05,874 --> 00:19:07,709
Isn't that what's real?

311
00:19:09,086 --> 00:19:10,254
No.

312
00:19:10,337 --> 00:19:14,132
Eating together, worrying together,

313
00:19:14,216 --> 00:19:17,094
and staying by each other's side
when things are tough.

314
00:19:17,177 --> 00:19:18,553
That's what makes a real family.

315
00:19:19,763 --> 00:19:21,723
The meals we share every day are more real

316
00:19:21,807 --> 00:19:24,393
than the blood ties
those mothers believe in.

317
00:19:24,476 --> 00:19:25,352
Got that?

318
00:19:28,438 --> 00:19:31,108
There are special families like us.

319
00:19:35,028 --> 00:19:36,196
So

320
00:19:36,738 --> 00:19:38,907
keep your chin up, shoulders back,

321
00:19:40,784 --> 00:19:42,869
and flash the world a smile!

322
00:19:45,998 --> 00:19:47,374
We'll dominate those slides.

323
00:19:47,457 --> 00:19:48,792
Let's go!

324
00:19:48,875 --> 00:19:50,669
Let's go!

325
00:20:03,974 --> 00:20:05,642
You scared me.

326
00:20:05,726 --> 00:20:07,102
Weren't you sleeping?

327
00:20:15,944 --> 00:20:17,821
What is it? You're scaring me.

328
00:20:19,656 --> 00:20:20,657
Ha-ri,

329
00:20:21,658 --> 00:20:23,285
let's give them the ledger.

330
00:20:28,832 --> 00:20:30,542
Then what about you?

331
00:20:32,044 --> 00:20:33,170
I know.

332
00:20:34,338 --> 00:20:35,672
I'll get punished for it.

333
00:20:38,508 --> 00:20:40,135
But I'm ready.

334
00:20:44,348 --> 00:20:46,391
Well, I'm not ready.

335
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:49,061
Ha-ri.

336
00:20:50,062 --> 00:20:54,024
I started this, so I have to end it.

337
00:20:54,107 --> 00:20:56,735
I should take responsibility
for my crimes.

338
00:20:56,818 --> 00:20:58,070
Let's hand over the ledger

339
00:20:58,653 --> 00:21:00,989
and help Mr. Park fight.

340
00:21:02,532 --> 00:21:03,784
Ha-jeong.

341
00:21:06,078 --> 00:21:09,998
Once this is over,
you'd better buckle down and study hard.

342
00:21:10,499 --> 00:21:12,250
I don't know what might happen to me,

343
00:21:12,751 --> 00:21:15,420
so you might really have
to take care of me then.

344
00:21:20,509 --> 00:21:21,385
All right.

345
00:21:22,886 --> 00:21:24,388
Let's give them the ledger.

346
00:21:38,527 --> 00:21:39,528
Boss!

347
00:21:44,741 --> 00:21:46,076
You've been through so much.

348
00:21:49,830 --> 00:21:51,123
How is our family?

349
00:21:52,249 --> 00:21:53,417
Everyone's doing fine.

350
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:55,127
They're all waiting for you.

351
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:57,754
I was able to hold on thanks to you.

352
00:21:57,838 --> 00:22:01,508
Even after all that fuss,
they released you right away.

353
00:22:02,342 --> 00:22:06,054
That just means
it's going to be worse out here.

354
00:22:06,596 --> 00:22:07,597
Let's go.

355
00:22:11,977 --> 00:22:14,312
The fraud Park Hae-kang must leave!

356
00:22:14,396 --> 00:22:17,357
-Leave True Value!
-Leave True Value!

357
00:22:17,441 --> 00:22:19,401
The fraud Park Hae-kang must leave!

358
00:22:19,484 --> 00:22:22,070
-Leave True Value!
-Leave True Value!

359
00:22:22,154 --> 00:22:25,240
The fraud Park Hae-kang must leave!

360
00:22:25,323 --> 00:22:27,033
-Leave True Value!
-Leave True Value!

361
00:22:27,701 --> 00:22:29,119
The thief is coming!

362
00:22:29,202 --> 00:22:33,415
The fraud who made a fake family
to steal from us is coming!

363
00:22:38,253 --> 00:22:40,088
Calm down, everyone!

364
00:22:40,172 --> 00:22:43,884
If you were investigated for embezzlement,
you should be coming out in handcuffs.

365
00:22:43,967 --> 00:22:45,427
How did you get released so quickly?

366
00:22:45,510 --> 00:22:47,971
Did you hire a powerful lawyer
with the 17.8 billion?

367
00:22:48,054 --> 00:22:50,015
-You thief!
-You thief!

368
00:22:55,061 --> 00:22:57,314
Stop! That's enough!

369
00:22:57,397 --> 00:22:58,815
-Enough?
-Enough?

370
00:22:58,899 --> 00:23:01,484
Did you forget what you did to us?

371
00:23:17,042 --> 00:23:18,793
I'll bill you 8,000 won

372
00:23:18,877 --> 00:23:20,045
for the umbrella later.

373
00:23:20,629 --> 00:23:23,173
Your timing with that umbrella
was a little late.

374
00:23:28,595 --> 00:23:29,721
This is ridiculous.

375
00:23:29,804 --> 00:23:32,224
They don't even know how precious salt is.

376
00:23:32,307 --> 00:23:33,808
Do you think the law is a joke?

377
00:23:33,892 --> 00:23:35,810
They let him go
because they found no evidence.

378
00:23:35,894 --> 00:23:37,354
What do you think you're doing?

379
00:23:37,437 --> 00:23:39,689
Look who's talking.

380
00:23:39,773 --> 00:23:41,358
You shameless assholes.

381
00:24:04,589 --> 00:24:06,383
Let me use it too. It's salty.

382
00:24:07,217 --> 00:24:08,802
How can you live with yourselves?

383
00:24:10,887 --> 00:24:12,973
-You're still pretending to be a couple?
-Seriously.

384
00:24:13,056 --> 00:24:15,517
How can you live with yourselves
after making a fake family

385
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:16,476
and stealing from us?

386
00:24:16,559 --> 00:24:19,229
Don't you dare run away with our money!

387
00:24:19,312 --> 00:24:21,564
-Don't you dare!
-You thief!

388
00:24:29,531 --> 00:24:31,074
I won't run away.

389
00:24:32,367 --> 00:24:34,411
I have no intention
of running away with my family.

390
00:24:35,328 --> 00:24:36,621
I'm staying right here

391
00:24:36,705 --> 00:24:39,332
until we catch the one
who took the 17.8 billion.

392
00:24:39,416 --> 00:24:40,500
What?

393
00:24:40,583 --> 00:24:42,252
Catch who? You're the thief!

394
00:24:43,211 --> 00:24:46,965
But if anyone harms my family
in the process,

395
00:24:47,590 --> 00:24:49,592
I'll make them pay in my own way.

396
00:24:50,343 --> 00:24:53,471
You've seen the posters,
so you know what kind of person I am.

397
00:24:54,306 --> 00:24:55,265
Goodness.

398
00:24:59,185 --> 00:25:01,855
If you want to find your money,
move aside.

399
00:25:19,372 --> 00:25:21,333
Mr. Choi, drink this.

400
00:25:21,416 --> 00:25:25,128
Come on. You need to eat to survive.

401
00:25:25,211 --> 00:25:26,421
No.

402
00:25:28,006 --> 00:25:29,007
Just drink it!

403
00:25:29,674 --> 00:25:30,884
Just drink it.

404
00:25:31,885 --> 00:25:33,261
Geez!

405
00:25:34,387 --> 00:25:36,473
-What are you doing here?
-Boss!

406
00:25:36,556 --> 00:25:38,683
-President Park!
-Boss!

407
00:25:38,767 --> 00:25:40,310
I missed you, Boss.

408
00:25:41,561 --> 00:25:43,271
You've gotten so thin.

409
00:25:45,899 --> 00:25:47,275
What's going on here?

410
00:25:47,359 --> 00:25:50,695
I went to talk to Mr. Choi for a moment,

411
00:25:50,779 --> 00:25:52,530
and we ran into each other.

412
00:25:52,614 --> 00:25:54,282
But he won't say anything.

413
00:25:54,366 --> 00:25:57,077
President Park! Please help me.

414
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,496
They'll be looking everywhere
for me right now.

415
00:25:59,579 --> 00:26:01,748
You jerk. You're the reason our boss…

416
00:26:01,831 --> 00:26:03,333
I'm sorry, President Park.

417
00:26:03,416 --> 00:26:05,960
But please help me.

418
00:26:07,462 --> 00:26:10,799
I'm not going anywhere
until Mr. Choi tells me

419
00:26:10,882 --> 00:26:13,009
where the 17.8 billion went.

420
00:26:13,093 --> 00:26:16,221
We have to prove that you're innocent,

421
00:26:16,304 --> 00:26:18,973
and that's the only way
we'll get our money back.

422
00:26:19,057 --> 00:26:21,476
Don't you agree? Gosh.

423
00:26:22,394 --> 00:26:23,228
Ms. Jang.

424
00:26:25,688 --> 00:26:28,650
Why would you go to such lengths for me?

425
00:26:29,943 --> 00:26:31,319
Why? Isn't it obvious?

426
00:26:32,070 --> 00:26:36,074
I know better than anyone
that you're innocent.

427
00:26:36,741 --> 00:26:38,326
I'm not innocent.

428
00:26:39,369 --> 00:26:40,453
I…

429
00:26:41,162 --> 00:26:43,123
didn't come here to protect
the apartment complex.

430
00:26:44,499 --> 00:26:45,750
What are you saying?

431
00:26:46,918 --> 00:26:48,086
It's true

432
00:26:49,170 --> 00:26:51,423
that I came here to embezzle the fund.

433
00:26:54,134 --> 00:26:55,385
Oh my gosh.

434
00:26:55,468 --> 00:26:58,054
Then you mean…

435
00:26:58,638 --> 00:27:00,432
it's true

436
00:27:01,015 --> 00:27:02,475
that you embezzled

437
00:27:03,435 --> 00:27:04,644
the 17.8 billion won?

438
00:27:05,228 --> 00:27:06,104
No.

439
00:27:06,729 --> 00:27:10,316
When I became the president,
the account was already empty.

440
00:27:12,402 --> 00:27:14,028
What are you talking about?

441
00:27:14,612 --> 00:27:17,615
You came to embezzle the fund,
but it was already taken?

442
00:27:18,700 --> 00:27:19,534
Goodness.

443
00:27:20,660 --> 00:27:23,371
That means Mr. Choi and President Seo

444
00:27:23,455 --> 00:27:26,541
already embezzled it together, doesn't it?

445
00:27:27,208 --> 00:27:28,334
Lee Chung-won.

446
00:27:29,544 --> 00:27:31,546
Taesan Construction's president.

447
00:27:32,964 --> 00:27:35,049
Who's that? Taesan Construction?

448
00:27:35,133 --> 00:27:36,926
The one who built our apartment complex?

449
00:27:39,888 --> 00:27:41,055
Are you sure?

450
00:27:42,056 --> 00:27:43,057
Yes.

451
00:27:45,477 --> 00:27:46,895
Those assholes!

452
00:27:46,978 --> 00:27:48,688
They took all our money.

453
00:27:49,522 --> 00:27:50,523
Ms. Jang.

454
00:27:52,567 --> 00:27:53,443
I'm sorry.

455
00:27:57,322 --> 00:27:58,573
President Park,

456
00:27:58,656 --> 00:28:01,284
I've seen how hard you've worked

457
00:28:01,367 --> 00:28:03,703
for our apartment complex.

458
00:28:03,786 --> 00:28:04,829
I believe

459
00:28:05,997 --> 00:28:07,207
all of that was sincere.

460
00:28:07,290 --> 00:28:09,209
None of that was fake.

461
00:28:09,292 --> 00:28:10,168
Right?

462
00:28:10,251 --> 00:28:12,086
So let's use your competence

463
00:28:12,587 --> 00:28:14,756
to find that 17.8 billion won.

464
00:28:15,340 --> 00:28:16,341
Find it for us.

465
00:28:17,383 --> 00:28:19,385
I won't let you leave True Value

466
00:28:19,469 --> 00:28:22,222
until we find that money.

467
00:28:23,389 --> 00:28:24,641
Understand?

468
00:28:36,110 --> 00:28:38,196
Yes, Ms. Jang.

469
00:28:44,035 --> 00:28:47,038
They used cheap spray paint.
This is so hard to remove.

470
00:28:48,039 --> 00:28:51,251
Gyeong-buk, forget this one.
See the "fraud" at the top?

471
00:28:51,334 --> 00:28:54,212
Shoot that instead.

472
00:28:54,295 --> 00:28:55,129
Okay.

473
00:28:58,132 --> 00:28:59,384
Dad!

474
00:29:00,343 --> 00:29:01,427
Dad?

475
00:29:02,303 --> 00:29:03,513
-What are you doing?
-Mr. Park!

476
00:29:03,596 --> 00:29:05,890
You're finally back.

477
00:29:05,974 --> 00:29:07,350
You look really thin.

478
00:29:07,433 --> 00:29:08,309
PARK HAE-KANG
FRAUD

479
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,729
Well…

480
00:29:11,813 --> 00:29:14,607
Our door is very popular right now.

481
00:29:15,441 --> 00:29:19,320
Uncle, I'm almost done
erasing the word "thief."

482
00:29:19,404 --> 00:29:20,947
Only the first letter is left.

483
00:29:25,493 --> 00:29:27,996
They did a tacky job, didn't they?

484
00:29:29,539 --> 00:29:30,707
Let's go inside. I'm hungry.

485
00:29:30,790 --> 00:29:31,958
Right. You must be hungry.

486
00:29:33,459 --> 00:29:36,004
-My fingerprint isn't working.
-It's not locked.

487
00:29:39,507 --> 00:29:41,259
That's so cold.

488
00:29:41,342 --> 00:29:43,344
Pull me out! Help me!

489
00:29:43,428 --> 00:29:45,805
Pull me up.

490
00:29:45,889 --> 00:29:47,932
Help…

491
00:29:50,435 --> 00:29:52,103
-Geez!
-You can't just leave me like this!

492
00:29:53,730 --> 00:29:54,731
What is all this?

493
00:29:54,814 --> 00:29:56,774
-When did you make all this?
-This is for you.

494
00:29:56,858 --> 00:29:58,735
How do you know how to make all of this?

495
00:29:58,818 --> 00:30:00,653
Everything is so white, though.

496
00:30:00,737 --> 00:30:02,614
This is going to blind my eyes.

497
00:30:02,697 --> 00:30:04,532
He put so much effort into this.

498
00:30:04,616 --> 00:30:06,284
He went through a whole sack of beans

499
00:30:06,367 --> 00:30:08,995
to make all this tofu
and help his boss get a fresh new start.

500
00:30:09,078 --> 00:30:11,581
It's all made with Korean soybeans.
They cost quite a bit.

501
00:30:11,664 --> 00:30:13,041
So make sure to eat everything.

502
00:30:13,124 --> 00:30:15,501
Right. Soybeans are called
the beef of the fields.

503
00:30:15,585 --> 00:30:16,878
Eat up, Mr. Park.

504
00:30:16,961 --> 00:30:21,674
You must have taken in a ton of sodium
from all the salt thrown at you.

505
00:30:21,758 --> 00:30:23,343
That's why we didn't season it.

506
00:30:24,552 --> 00:30:25,803
Enjoy.

507
00:30:25,887 --> 00:30:30,058
With all that red graffiti
and the salt thrown at you,

508
00:30:30,141 --> 00:30:32,352
you need this to cleanse your insides.

509
00:30:32,435 --> 00:30:34,729
You should regain your strength
and start over.

510
00:30:34,812 --> 00:30:37,941
You know, I wonder
if being in a gang is meant for me.

511
00:30:38,024 --> 00:30:40,443
Whenever I see white tofu,
it reminds me of the old days.

512
00:30:40,526 --> 00:30:41,569
Do you have soy sauce?

513
00:30:41,653 --> 00:30:44,656
Just eat whatever is given to you today.

514
00:30:44,739 --> 00:30:46,199
All right, Big Guy.

515
00:30:46,282 --> 00:30:47,533
Sorry.

516
00:30:48,952 --> 00:30:51,871
Uncle, I'll eat a lot and grow stronger

517
00:30:51,955 --> 00:30:55,249
so I can defeat all the bad guys for you.

518
00:30:56,918 --> 00:30:57,919
Okay.

519
00:30:58,503 --> 00:31:00,129
When you got taken by the police,

520
00:31:00,213 --> 00:31:02,924
I was going to come out
and handle everything,

521
00:31:03,007 --> 00:31:05,301
but she stopped me.

522
00:31:05,385 --> 00:31:06,636
You were hiding in the closet.

523
00:31:07,345 --> 00:31:08,471
You saw me?

524
00:31:08,554 --> 00:31:10,056
That's why he's the Lizard.

525
00:31:13,476 --> 00:31:14,769
-This is good.
-It's tasty.

526
00:31:14,852 --> 00:31:16,020
It's good.

527
00:31:22,860 --> 00:31:24,862
-Here.
-What are you doing?

528
00:31:34,539 --> 00:31:36,916
TRANSACTION LEDGER

529
00:31:38,418 --> 00:31:39,502
You just took the ledger

530
00:31:39,585 --> 00:31:41,254
out of the bookshelf?

531
00:31:41,754 --> 00:31:43,923
Yes. I told you I hid it in a safe place.

532
00:31:44,507 --> 00:31:45,717
How is this a safe place?

533
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:48,636
What if Gyeong-nam took out a book
to read for Gyeong-buk and--

534
00:31:48,720 --> 00:31:50,054
You think he'd do that?

535
00:31:50,138 --> 00:31:53,391
These books are so new,
the bindings crack every time I open them.

536
00:31:55,309 --> 00:31:57,520
You're right. This was the safest place.

537
00:32:02,942 --> 00:32:04,485
My sister said she's ready.

538
00:32:04,569 --> 00:32:07,155
She'll take responsibility for her crimes.

539
00:32:11,451 --> 00:32:13,161
I know this wasn't…

540
00:32:15,288 --> 00:32:16,372
an easy decision.

541
00:32:17,290 --> 00:32:20,752
I'm putting my sister's life on the line
by giving this to you.

542
00:32:21,544 --> 00:32:24,464
So make sure to crush them

543
00:32:25,381 --> 00:32:27,717
so my sister won't have gone
to prison for nothing.

544
00:32:55,036 --> 00:32:57,872
PARKING GARAGE FAN INSPECTION
(NOT CONDUCTED)

545
00:33:01,042 --> 00:33:04,170
PARKING GARAGE LIGHT REPLACEMENT
(REDUCED QUANTITY)

546
00:33:13,179 --> 00:33:15,181
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN

547
00:33:15,890 --> 00:33:19,185
I'm so happy to be preparing meals
for a criminal who tried to run away.

548
00:33:20,311 --> 00:33:21,145
Gosh.

549
00:33:21,729 --> 00:33:23,523
There's too much sauce on this.

550
00:33:26,025 --> 00:33:27,527
Open up, Mr. Choi.

551
00:33:28,027 --> 00:33:29,362
Here comes the airplane.

552
00:33:31,739 --> 00:33:35,159
I told you I have high cholesterol.

553
00:33:35,243 --> 00:33:38,329
Give me some spinach instead of ham.

554
00:33:38,412 --> 00:33:41,916
And I have trouble digesting
anything that isn't organic.

555
00:33:41,999 --> 00:33:44,669
Mr. Choi, this isn't a fancy restaurant.

556
00:33:44,752 --> 00:33:47,630
Big Guy, what happens
to picky eaters here?

557
00:33:47,713 --> 00:33:49,674
We take them to the rooftop.

558
00:33:49,757 --> 00:33:52,385
-And?
-And they're put in a luggage bag.

559
00:33:52,468 --> 00:33:54,637
Fine, I'll eat.

560
00:33:57,557 --> 00:33:59,267
Eat up. Chew thoroughly.

561
00:34:01,227 --> 00:34:02,854
It's a bit salty.

562
00:34:02,937 --> 00:34:04,564
I've been on a low-sodium diet.

563
00:34:05,148 --> 00:34:07,567
-Who wants more?
-Me!

564
00:34:07,650 --> 00:34:09,610
Just eat up before I take everything away.

565
00:34:09,694 --> 00:34:12,697
You should be worried about your life,
not your cholesterol.

566
00:34:12,780 --> 00:34:14,073
I'm sorry.

567
00:34:16,159 --> 00:34:17,326
-Boss.
-Boss.

568
00:34:17,869 --> 00:34:19,453
-You're here.
-Hello, Boss.

569
00:34:26,419 --> 00:34:27,378
Mr. Choi.

570
00:34:28,254 --> 00:34:30,756
The ledger that Ms. Kang Ha-jeong kept

571
00:34:31,424 --> 00:34:34,427
only contains
President Seo's name and yours.

572
00:34:35,303 --> 00:34:37,722
The notes she wrote
after the embezzled amounts

573
00:34:37,805 --> 00:34:39,849
just say,

574
00:34:39,932 --> 00:34:43,603
"delivered to the facility manager"
or "delivered to President Seo."

575
00:34:43,686 --> 00:34:45,855
Lee Chung-won's name
doesn't appear anywhere.

576
00:34:46,814 --> 00:34:49,233
Do you know what that means?

577
00:34:50,067 --> 00:34:54,238
Who do you think the police will come for
when this is released?

578
00:34:55,072 --> 00:34:57,992
But President Seo is gone from this world.

579
00:34:58,075 --> 00:35:01,913
So the sole culprit
who pocketed the entire 17.8 billion

580
00:35:01,996 --> 00:35:03,456
will be you, Mr. Choi.

581
00:35:07,293 --> 00:35:08,127
No way.

582
00:35:09,378 --> 00:35:11,214
Lee Chung-won will make that happen.

583
00:35:13,716 --> 00:35:15,509
All he needs is for you to be gone.

584
00:35:17,845 --> 00:35:19,680
Once he gets his hands on this ledger,

585
00:35:20,473 --> 00:35:22,183
he'll be innocent.

586
00:35:27,772 --> 00:35:28,814
What…

587
00:35:29,565 --> 00:35:30,650
Then…

588
00:35:31,192 --> 00:35:32,652
What should I do?

589
00:35:37,782 --> 00:35:40,910
There's been a lot of talk
about Taesan's kindergarten incident.

590
00:35:41,661 --> 00:35:43,246
Get Juan and Hanmin included

591
00:35:43,329 --> 00:35:45,498
in the Oman New Town consortium.

592
00:35:46,082 --> 00:35:47,833
Juan and Hanmin?

593
00:35:48,960 --> 00:35:52,088
Aren't they run by old geezers
who only care about background?

594
00:35:52,922 --> 00:35:56,342
Why would I include them
in something I set up?

595
00:35:57,218 --> 00:36:00,554
We're not telling you to sit and watch.
We're saying you need insurance.

596
00:36:00,638 --> 00:36:02,265
The Oman New Town project

597
00:36:02,348 --> 00:36:05,268
is too big for you to handle on your own.

598
00:36:06,352 --> 00:36:08,271
Don't you trust me?

599
00:36:09,438 --> 00:36:11,691
Ever since I worked in demolition,

600
00:36:12,191 --> 00:36:15,820
I've been great
at tearing down other people's lives.

601
00:36:15,903 --> 00:36:18,281
But I'm even better at building things.

602
00:36:20,074 --> 00:36:22,702
A single excavator is enough
to take care of this.

603
00:36:23,369 --> 00:36:25,788
I don't get why you keep making a fuss.

604
00:36:25,871 --> 00:36:28,791
You need a background
in the construction industry, Mr. Lee.

605
00:36:28,874 --> 00:36:32,461
The smell of the steel pipe
you used to hold still hasn't faded.

606
00:36:34,964 --> 00:36:37,383
I have a pile of documents

607
00:36:37,466 --> 00:36:40,928
on how those people
who care so much about background

608
00:36:41,012 --> 00:36:43,514
funneled slush funds
through their sons' development companies.

609
00:36:43,597 --> 00:36:46,767
Such documents don't mean anything to us.

610
00:36:47,351 --> 00:36:49,562
Risk management is more important.

611
00:36:49,645 --> 00:36:50,604
Mr. Lee.

612
00:36:51,230 --> 00:36:54,525
Let me put it more simply
so you can understand.

613
00:36:54,608 --> 00:36:56,902
You're nothing but a spare tire to us.

614
00:36:56,986 --> 00:36:59,113
A replacement for when things go wrong.

615
00:37:06,245 --> 00:37:10,124
You're really hurting my feelings.

616
00:37:10,750 --> 00:37:12,501
Don't take it personally.

617
00:37:12,585 --> 00:37:16,964
We have to worry
about our entire nation, you know.

618
00:37:17,048 --> 00:37:19,091
As long as you work smart,

619
00:37:19,175 --> 00:37:23,387
that spare tire
will keep sitting in our trunk.

620
00:37:24,305 --> 00:37:26,349
There's talk about shoddy construction.

621
00:37:26,432 --> 00:37:28,851
Shouldn't you handle that issue first?

622
00:37:34,815 --> 00:37:37,068
All right.

623
00:37:37,860 --> 00:37:40,321
You can watch how I handle it…

624
00:37:41,614 --> 00:37:42,990
tomorrow.

625
00:37:57,797 --> 00:38:00,549
The patient's condition has worsened.
Contact his guardian.

626
00:38:00,633 --> 00:38:01,675
I'll contact him now.

627
00:38:02,426 --> 00:38:03,469
Don't.

628
00:38:04,261 --> 00:38:05,179
What?

629
00:38:05,805 --> 00:38:08,557
Don't call Park Hae-kang.

630
00:38:09,642 --> 00:38:10,851
He's busy.

631
00:38:11,560 --> 00:38:13,312
But we need your guardian's approval…

632
00:38:13,979 --> 00:38:15,106
"Guardian"?

633
00:38:16,565 --> 00:38:20,361
I'm his guardian,
not the other way around.

634
00:38:20,444 --> 00:38:22,571
I told you, don't call him…

635
00:38:35,584 --> 00:38:37,837
Good evening, Mr. Son.

636
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:39,463
You scared me.

637
00:38:41,424 --> 00:38:44,718
I have something to discuss with you
before you go.

638
00:38:45,219 --> 00:38:47,054
There's nothing to discuss.

639
00:38:47,721 --> 00:38:50,474
You didn't bring me a single penny,
let alone ten billion.

640
00:38:51,350 --> 00:38:52,309
This…

641
00:38:53,018 --> 00:38:55,229
is much more valuable than that.

642
00:38:59,108 --> 00:39:01,777
Evidence on Taesan's shoddy construction.

643
00:39:05,573 --> 00:39:06,866
Shoddy construction?

644
00:39:07,741 --> 00:39:08,868
Hey.

645
00:39:08,951 --> 00:39:12,204
Have you ever seen a construction company
in Korea go under for that?

646
00:39:13,205 --> 00:39:14,999
They'll pay a fine, and that's it.

647
00:39:15,082 --> 00:39:17,001
It's not about going under.

648
00:39:17,501 --> 00:39:18,961
It's about becoming useless.

649
00:39:19,587 --> 00:39:21,547
Once Taesan hits the headlines for this

650
00:39:21,630 --> 00:39:23,048
and the president faces the press,

651
00:39:24,175 --> 00:39:25,885
the One Club will collapse.

652
00:39:27,928 --> 00:39:28,888
What?

653
00:39:28,971 --> 00:39:31,474
Your ticket to join the club is gone.

654
00:39:32,308 --> 00:39:34,935
How long will you keep rowing
on a sinking ship?

655
00:39:35,978 --> 00:39:37,771
Use this evidence to climb a new ladder

656
00:39:37,855 --> 00:39:41,233
as a detective who took down
a conglomerate president.

657
00:39:41,317 --> 00:39:44,236
What better gift could there be
for the commissioner?

658
00:39:44,320 --> 00:39:48,282
You're holding leverage
that could rattle Lee Chung-won.

659
00:39:56,665 --> 00:39:58,918
Can you really rattle Lee Chung-won?

660
00:40:00,002 --> 00:40:01,670
I'm going to bring him down.

661
00:40:02,379 --> 00:40:05,633
So stop holding my old boss hostage

662
00:40:06,175 --> 00:40:07,927
and release him on medical bail.

663
00:40:18,229 --> 00:40:20,272
I'll decide once I see the results.

664
00:40:48,342 --> 00:40:51,387
Why are you looking at me so sadly?

665
00:40:52,596 --> 00:40:54,056
You're making me uncomfortable.

666
00:40:55,474 --> 00:40:56,433
I wasn't.

667
00:40:58,644 --> 00:41:00,813
I was glaring at you viciously.

668
00:41:02,523 --> 00:41:04,358
Don't look so glum.

669
00:41:05,776 --> 00:41:07,444
You're not the one dying.

670
00:41:08,779 --> 00:41:09,863
I'm not looking glum.

671
00:41:10,739 --> 00:41:12,616
I look really handsome right now.

672
00:41:15,869 --> 00:41:17,246
Take good care of yourself.

673
00:41:18,330 --> 00:41:20,833
You're still young.
You should stay in shape.

674
00:41:25,129 --> 00:41:26,589
Is something wrong?

675
00:41:30,301 --> 00:41:31,594
No, of course not.

676
00:41:32,469 --> 00:41:34,722
I'm just sorry
I couldn't get you released quickly.

677
00:41:37,099 --> 00:41:38,809
You're not going to tell me

678
00:41:39,893 --> 00:41:41,729
what you're up to?

679
00:41:43,397 --> 00:41:44,273
I…

680
00:41:45,232 --> 00:41:48,944
chose someone else instead of you.

681
00:41:50,404 --> 00:41:51,322
Mr. Park.

682
00:41:52,197 --> 00:41:53,407
Please…

683
00:41:53,490 --> 00:41:55,576
Please help my sister.

684
00:41:57,911 --> 00:42:00,914
Is she young and pretty?

685
00:42:04,793 --> 00:42:05,961
It's not like that.

686
00:42:08,547 --> 00:42:11,091
Well, I'm old and not pretty.

687
00:42:11,592 --> 00:42:15,304
It's natural for me
to be pushed down the priority list.

688
00:42:15,387 --> 00:42:16,930
You did the right thing.

689
00:42:19,516 --> 00:42:21,435
You'll be released soon.

690
00:42:23,354 --> 00:42:24,938
I'm working on it,

691
00:42:25,939 --> 00:42:27,900
so hold on just a little while longer.

692
00:42:35,074 --> 00:42:36,492
You know,

693
00:42:37,868 --> 00:42:41,622
you're a man who instinctively judges
what's right or wrong.

694
00:42:43,040 --> 00:42:45,668
You pretend to be a bad guy,

695
00:42:46,418 --> 00:42:49,046
but you've got a better heart than anyone.

696
00:42:50,422 --> 00:42:51,340
No.

697
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:54,426
I do a lot of bad things.

698
00:42:54,510 --> 00:42:55,678
I am a bad guy.

699
00:42:57,137 --> 00:43:02,059
You're the type to save people
even if you planned to do something bad.

700
00:43:03,268 --> 00:43:04,853
I know you.

701
00:43:06,063 --> 00:43:07,022
So…

702
00:43:08,774 --> 00:43:11,777
do whatever you want.

703
00:43:12,986 --> 00:43:15,781
There's no need to hesitate because of me.

704
00:43:15,864 --> 00:43:19,368
And don't make bad choices
because of me either.

705
00:43:19,952 --> 00:43:23,163
If I become an obstacle
to what you're trying to do,

706
00:43:23,872 --> 00:43:28,127
I won't be able to rest in peace.

707
00:43:29,002 --> 00:43:29,837
Geez.

708
00:43:29,920 --> 00:43:31,839
Why do you keep talking about dying?

709
00:43:32,798 --> 00:43:34,383
You should enjoy life by my side first.

710
00:43:34,466 --> 00:43:36,677
So quit the nonsense and stay strong.

711
00:43:37,636 --> 00:43:40,973
I won't let you go like this.

712
00:43:42,516 --> 00:43:43,767
You punk.

713
00:43:45,811 --> 00:43:49,565
You've been through a lot
being my son all these years.

714
00:43:53,235 --> 00:43:54,653
Thank you.

715
00:43:59,742 --> 00:44:01,869
You're making me cringe. I'm leaving.

716
00:44:02,911 --> 00:44:04,496
Make sure to eat well.

717
00:44:06,540 --> 00:44:08,459
I love you, son.

718
00:44:40,824 --> 00:44:44,953
WE SINCERELY APOLOGIZE
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION

719
00:44:50,125 --> 00:44:53,504
What are they up to,
calling all these reporters here?

720
00:44:53,587 --> 00:44:55,422
-What's going on?
-You didn't hear anything?

721
00:44:55,506 --> 00:44:57,049
They never said anything.

722
00:44:57,132 --> 00:44:58,175
Let's see what they say.

723
00:44:58,258 --> 00:44:59,551
Sure, let's see.

724
00:45:12,606 --> 00:45:15,734
Isn't he the guy who rode
the elevator with us last time?

725
00:45:15,817 --> 00:45:17,277
Yes, the penthouse.

726
00:45:17,361 --> 00:45:19,488
-He's the president of Taesan.
-No way.

727
00:45:19,571 --> 00:45:21,031
You didn't know, right?

728
00:45:21,114 --> 00:45:23,951
Is there a specific reason
why you're apologizing here

729
00:45:24,034 --> 00:45:25,661
instead of at the company headquarters?

730
00:45:25,744 --> 00:45:28,121
Some are saying
this is just a show for the cameras.

731
00:45:28,205 --> 00:45:29,414
Give us a comment.

732
00:45:38,465 --> 00:45:39,716
I am standing here today…

733
00:45:41,885 --> 00:45:43,303
not as Taesan's president,

734
00:45:44,555 --> 00:45:47,975
but as a resident of True Value State.

735
00:45:49,017 --> 00:45:50,227
I believe it is my duty

736
00:45:50,310 --> 00:45:53,605
to apologize at the location
where my neighbors and their children

737
00:45:54,231 --> 00:45:55,816
could have been harmed.

738
00:45:55,899 --> 00:45:56,984
An apology isn't enough!

739
00:45:57,067 --> 00:45:59,194
Our kids almost died, you fraud!

740
00:45:59,278 --> 00:46:02,197
How can you build
a kindergarten like that?

741
00:46:02,281 --> 00:46:04,116
Don't you even have a family?

742
00:46:06,785 --> 00:46:08,245
The investigation

743
00:46:08,745 --> 00:46:11,415
found that our subcontractor
used improper construction methods

744
00:46:11,498 --> 00:46:13,333
and failed to oversee the work properly.

745
00:46:13,417 --> 00:46:16,753
Are you blaming everything
on your subcontractor?

746
00:46:16,837 --> 00:46:19,923
It's Taesan's fault for not managing
the construction properly.

747
00:46:20,007 --> 00:46:22,217
Don't you dare make excuses!

748
00:46:24,636 --> 00:46:26,305
How shameless!

749
00:46:27,556 --> 00:46:28,765
You're absolutely right.

750
00:46:29,850 --> 00:46:30,934
It was my oversight.

751
00:46:32,894 --> 00:46:36,148
That is why Taesan
has made a major decision.

752
00:46:36,857 --> 00:46:38,859
We will demolish
the kindergarten immediately

753
00:46:38,942 --> 00:46:41,445
and rebuild it
into one of the finest kindergartens

754
00:46:41,528 --> 00:46:43,614
with Korea's top architects.

755
00:46:45,032 --> 00:46:47,993
-That will take ages.
-That'll take forever.

756
00:46:48,660 --> 00:46:50,537
And during the construction period,

757
00:46:50,621 --> 00:46:54,249
I'll send our children
to a top-tier English kindergarten nearby.

758
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:58,253
And of course,
Taesan will pay for the tuition

759
00:46:58,337 --> 00:47:00,505
and the shuttle bus fees.

760
00:47:01,006 --> 00:47:02,758
Their tuition
is over three million a month.

761
00:47:02,841 --> 00:47:05,719
-Three million? That's insane.
-It's very expensive.

762
00:47:05,802 --> 00:47:08,430
Taesan promises to take care

763
00:47:09,931 --> 00:47:11,767
of our children's safety and education.

764
00:47:11,850 --> 00:47:13,393
Once again, we apologize.

765
00:47:13,477 --> 00:47:14,645
We ask for your trust.

766
00:47:19,024 --> 00:47:21,485
At least they're taking responsibility.

767
00:47:21,568 --> 00:47:25,113
Right. Sending them
to an English kindergarten changes things.

768
00:47:25,197 --> 00:47:26,573
-What now?
-We should trust them.

769
00:47:26,657 --> 00:47:29,326
-Do we give them another chance?
-This doesn't feel right.

770
00:47:31,286 --> 00:47:32,746
Trust them? Are you kidding me?

771
00:47:55,644 --> 00:47:57,062
President Park…

772
00:47:57,145 --> 00:47:59,523
What's he doing? Why is he holding that?

773
00:47:59,606 --> 00:48:00,482
Do we call the cops?

774
00:48:02,109 --> 00:48:03,360
What is that?

775
00:48:04,194 --> 00:48:05,612
President Lee Chung-won.

776
00:48:06,405 --> 00:48:08,156
Do you think
building another kindergarten…

777
00:48:11,201 --> 00:48:12,703
will solve everything?

778
00:48:14,329 --> 00:48:15,539
-Open the door!
-Open this!

779
00:48:16,164 --> 00:48:17,999
Je-gil, can't you hurry up?

780
00:48:18,083 --> 00:48:20,377
-They'll break down the door at this rate!
-Almost done.

781
00:48:20,460 --> 00:48:21,795
He always says that.

782
00:48:22,337 --> 00:48:24,506
He's right in front of Lee Chung-won now.

783
00:48:27,384 --> 00:48:28,635
LIVE BROADCAST IN PROGRESS

784
00:48:28,719 --> 00:48:32,556
Yes! Every wall pad, elevator display,
and even the emergency speakers

785
00:48:32,639 --> 00:48:33,724
are connected now.

786
00:48:34,307 --> 00:48:35,142
Boss.

787
00:48:35,225 --> 00:48:37,310
Everyone in this apartment complex
is watching now!

788
00:48:38,895 --> 00:48:39,771
All right. Be careful.

789
00:48:41,857 --> 00:48:43,150
Watch out.

790
00:48:49,614 --> 00:48:50,907
Move!

791
00:48:56,037 --> 00:48:57,080
One.

792
00:49:00,500 --> 00:49:01,543
Two.

793
00:49:02,669 --> 00:49:05,255
How many times
do I need to hit it to tear it down?

794
00:49:06,840 --> 00:49:08,341
Wait, President Park!

795
00:49:19,311 --> 00:49:21,146
What's that doing there?

796
00:49:21,229 --> 00:49:22,773
It's filled with trash.

797
00:49:22,856 --> 00:49:23,940
What is that doing there?

798
00:49:25,108 --> 00:49:26,359
Where's the rebar?

799
00:49:29,529 --> 00:49:30,906
That must be from a garbage dump!

800
00:49:30,989 --> 00:49:33,867
Did they fill the walls with trash?

801
00:49:35,744 --> 00:49:39,331
Is there any construction in Korea
that isn't shoddy?

802
00:49:39,414 --> 00:49:41,792
They're actually all the same.

803
00:49:42,375 --> 00:49:43,710
Is shoddy construction

804
00:49:44,544 --> 00:49:45,670
something to brag about?

805
00:49:47,464 --> 00:49:49,508
This is the basement
mechanical room floor plan.

806
00:49:49,591 --> 00:49:52,093
The pipes go through here.

807
00:49:52,177 --> 00:49:53,428
It's right below this.

808
00:49:53,512 --> 00:49:54,763
-This place here.
-Right.

809
00:49:54,846 --> 00:49:57,516
This is likely
to have construction defects.

810
00:49:57,599 --> 00:49:59,851
Every part you can't see
was probably built poorly.

811
00:49:59,935 --> 00:50:01,520
Even if they leave out some rebar rods,

812
00:50:01,603 --> 00:50:04,189
people can't tell
if they're covered up nicely.

813
00:50:04,272 --> 00:50:07,192
It should be detecting the rebar,
but it's quiet.

814
00:50:07,275 --> 00:50:08,527
Shouldn't there be rebar here?

815
00:50:08,610 --> 00:50:09,736
Look.

816
00:50:09,820 --> 00:50:11,571
It's just crumbling like this.

817
00:50:11,655 --> 00:50:13,615
They only put rebar where it's visible.

818
00:50:14,115 --> 00:50:15,659
Where does this wall lead to?

819
00:50:15,742 --> 00:50:17,202
This connects all the way

820
00:50:17,285 --> 00:50:20,497
to the conference room's main wall.

821
00:50:24,334 --> 00:50:25,252
All right.

822
00:50:29,631 --> 00:50:31,007
Let me ask you one question.

823
00:50:31,591 --> 00:50:34,469
Are you going to demolish
all 9,800 apartments here

824
00:50:34,553 --> 00:50:35,720
and rebuild them again?

825
00:50:46,064 --> 00:50:47,440
President Lee Chung-won.

826
00:50:53,405 --> 00:50:57,784
Why do you think
you're being humiliated here?

827
00:50:57,868 --> 00:50:58,910
It's a quiz.

828
00:51:00,871 --> 00:51:01,746
Park Hae-kang.

829
00:51:02,789 --> 00:51:05,709
Do you even know what you've done?

830
00:51:06,501 --> 00:51:09,504
Number one, because Park Hae-kang
is crazier than expected.

831
00:51:10,171 --> 00:51:12,799
Number two, because you're
more careless than expected.

832
00:51:12,883 --> 00:51:14,092
Guess the answer.

833
00:51:15,260 --> 00:51:17,012
What's number three?

834
00:51:17,095 --> 00:51:18,471
Number three,

835
00:51:19,222 --> 00:51:22,100
because you got trapped
in your own narrative.

836
00:51:23,476 --> 00:51:25,270
And it's time for you to go down.

837
00:51:29,357 --> 00:51:31,401
Listen carefully.

838
00:51:31,484 --> 00:51:33,570
Now, when people hear
the name Lee Chung-won,

839
00:51:34,195 --> 00:51:36,031
they'll only think of shoddy construction,

840
00:51:36,114 --> 00:51:37,616
trash walls, and lies.

841
00:51:37,699 --> 00:51:40,201
They won't think of you any other way.

842
00:51:40,952 --> 00:51:44,247
Nobody will trust a word you say now.

843
00:51:52,839 --> 00:51:54,674
I'll treat you to soup later,

844
00:51:55,175 --> 00:51:57,052
with extra meat.

845
00:51:58,553 --> 00:51:59,596
President Lee!

846
00:51:59,679 --> 00:52:01,181
Will you take responsibility?

847
00:52:22,577 --> 00:52:25,580
How dare a lowlife thug do this to me?

848
00:52:29,793 --> 00:52:31,628
GONGYEONG DAILY LEE SANG-GYU

849
00:52:34,047 --> 00:52:35,757
Great timing.

850
00:52:37,467 --> 00:52:40,053
That video aired from the conference room…

851
00:52:40,679 --> 00:52:42,889
Make sure not a single article
is released about it.

852
00:52:42,973 --> 00:52:44,766
I'll give you as much as you want.

853
00:52:45,392 --> 00:52:47,686
The reporters at the scene
have already published articles.

854
00:52:47,769 --> 00:52:48,979
It's too late.

855
00:52:49,062 --> 00:52:51,398
"Taesan trash wall"
is the top trending search

856
00:52:51,481 --> 00:52:52,565
on every portal right now.

857
00:52:52,649 --> 00:52:54,317
Then get those articles taken down!

858
00:52:54,401 --> 00:52:56,486
Call the presidents of every portal.

859
00:52:56,569 --> 00:52:58,989
No, call the elders

860
00:52:59,072 --> 00:53:01,116
and stop all the articles!

861
00:53:01,199 --> 00:53:03,994
Everyone's releasing articles about it.
We can't afford to miss this.

862
00:53:04,077 --> 00:53:05,662
You crossed the line this time.

863
00:53:12,544 --> 00:53:14,337
Park Hae-kang, that bastard…

864
00:53:15,672 --> 00:53:17,882
He's really blowing everything up.

865
00:53:20,051 --> 00:53:21,428
TAESAN'S SHODDY CONSTRUCTION EXPOSED

866
00:53:21,511 --> 00:53:23,054
You all saw the video, right?

867
00:53:23,138 --> 00:53:26,766
Mr. Park came in
dragging that sledgehammer,

868
00:53:26,850 --> 00:53:28,643
dug his toes in,

869
00:53:28,727 --> 00:53:30,895
drew all his strength up from his core,

870
00:53:30,979 --> 00:53:33,648
then swung that sledgehammer like this

871
00:53:33,732 --> 00:53:37,235
and jumped, slamming it against the wall,

872
00:53:37,318 --> 00:53:40,363
and it came crumbling down
with a cloud of dust…

873
00:53:40,447 --> 00:53:43,116
And instead of the rebar,

874
00:53:43,199 --> 00:53:44,951
a load of trash

875
00:53:46,077 --> 00:53:47,287
came spilling out.

876
00:53:47,996 --> 00:53:50,915
That was the most amazing video
I've seen this year.

877
00:53:52,459 --> 00:53:56,129
He really is my son. That was so cool.

878
00:53:57,005 --> 00:53:59,466
Korea really is an internet powerhouse.

879
00:53:59,549 --> 00:54:00,925
The video's already going viral.

880
00:54:01,009 --> 00:54:03,178
Really? Wow!

881
00:54:03,261 --> 00:54:05,972
Would Taesan be able to survive this?

882
00:54:09,642 --> 00:54:11,728
-They're done for.
-They're done for.

883
00:54:11,811 --> 00:54:13,605
It's checkmate.

884
00:54:13,688 --> 00:54:15,607
Game, set, and match.

885
00:54:16,566 --> 00:54:17,817
There's no way out.

886
00:54:17,901 --> 00:54:19,986
Justice has been served.

887
00:54:20,070 --> 00:54:23,656
The hashtag "Taesan survivor"
is trending on social media

888
00:54:23,740 --> 00:54:27,452
as a protest against Taesan's
shoddy apartment construction.

889
00:54:27,535 --> 00:54:31,039
There are growing demands
for safety checks on all apartments…

890
00:54:31,122 --> 00:54:32,165
"Survivor"?

891
00:54:33,249 --> 00:54:36,211
They've been eating
and sleeping comfortably

892
00:54:36,294 --> 00:54:37,629
in the apartments I built,

893
00:54:38,797 --> 00:54:41,508
and now they're pretending to be victims?

894
00:54:41,591 --> 00:54:42,801
Sir,

895
00:54:43,510 --> 00:54:46,763
Taesan lost a trillion won in market value
just ten minutes into trading.

896
00:54:46,846 --> 00:54:48,973
Our treasury stock
won't be enough to stop the slide.

897
00:54:51,017 --> 00:54:54,187
This is all because you couldn't
even get rid of one lousy thug!

898
00:54:54,270 --> 00:54:55,313
I'm sorry, sir.

899
00:54:55,396 --> 00:54:58,858
Neither the media nor the prosecution
is willing to make a move right now.

900
00:55:06,116 --> 00:55:07,200
I see.

901
00:55:07,951 --> 00:55:09,494
All of them

902
00:55:10,453 --> 00:55:12,914
are hiding like cowards.

903
00:55:13,665 --> 00:55:14,791
Sir?

904
00:55:15,875 --> 00:55:19,129
If money won't solve this,
I'll change my methods.

905
00:55:20,046 --> 00:55:22,507
If a thug set this up…

906
00:55:24,259 --> 00:55:27,637
I should play by his rules
so I won't feel bad about it.

907
00:55:30,348 --> 00:55:31,724
Don't you agree, Mr. Kim?

908
00:55:39,357 --> 00:55:41,192
MR. SON, SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

909
00:55:44,737 --> 00:55:46,281
Did you see the news?

910
00:55:46,364 --> 00:55:48,700
You created quite the mess.

911
00:55:48,783 --> 00:55:50,535
I've just been summoned
by the commissioner.

912
00:55:51,452 --> 00:55:53,621
It's your turn to secure
the investigation into Taesan

913
00:55:53,705 --> 00:55:55,707
and become a hero.

914
00:55:56,207 --> 00:55:59,627
I'll make sure Lee Chung-won
ends up in front of the cameras,

915
00:55:59,711 --> 00:56:01,045
so you'd better watch your mouth.

916
00:56:01,629 --> 00:56:04,757
As long as my old boss is released,
I'll keep my mouth shut.

917
00:56:04,841 --> 00:56:06,885
All right.
I just submitted the paperwork for it.

918
00:56:06,968 --> 00:56:08,136
Get it done quickly.

919
00:56:16,144 --> 00:56:17,145
I'll answer it.

920
00:56:21,316 --> 00:56:23,443
Can you step out for a moment?

921
00:56:24,360 --> 00:56:26,654
Come on out. It's okay.

922
00:56:34,579 --> 00:56:36,080
What are you waiting for?

923
00:56:36,164 --> 00:56:38,958
You should say the lines you prepared.

924
00:56:39,042 --> 00:56:40,543
President Park,

925
00:56:40,627 --> 00:56:43,171
I'm sorry.

926
00:56:43,880 --> 00:56:45,131
We're sorry.

927
00:56:45,215 --> 00:56:48,259
-I apologize for throwing salt at you.
-I'm sorry.

928
00:56:48,343 --> 00:56:49,844
-We're sorry.
-We're sorry.

929
00:56:49,928 --> 00:56:51,888
-We were too much.
-We're sorry.

930
00:56:51,971 --> 00:56:53,389
-We apologize.
-We're sorry.

931
00:56:56,434 --> 00:56:58,144
Well, if you've apologized,

932
00:56:58,228 --> 00:57:00,271
you should get to the main point.

933
00:57:00,355 --> 00:57:01,689
President Park,

934
00:57:01,773 --> 00:57:04,400
everyone in our building has agreed

935
00:57:04,484 --> 00:57:06,694
to tear down all the walls
starting tomorrow.

936
00:57:06,778 --> 00:57:08,780
Our building agreed to do it too.

937
00:57:09,948 --> 00:57:11,282
And if you find trash inside?

938
00:57:12,909 --> 00:57:14,869
What if your property value drops?

939
00:57:14,953 --> 00:57:16,704
A safe home for our kids

940
00:57:16,788 --> 00:57:19,123
is more important than our property value.

941
00:57:19,624 --> 00:57:23,711
And you're the only one
who can bring Taesan down.

942
00:57:23,795 --> 00:57:25,880
So please take the lead.

943
00:57:25,964 --> 00:57:28,049
We'll support you.

944
00:57:28,132 --> 00:57:30,260
-Please, President Park.
-Please help us.

945
00:57:30,343 --> 00:57:31,427
Please help us.

946
00:57:31,511 --> 00:57:33,012
Please help us out.

947
00:57:33,596 --> 00:57:34,514
What was that?

948
00:57:34,597 --> 00:57:37,016
Please help us.

949
00:57:37,100 --> 00:57:39,269
-Help us.
-Give us a chance.

950
00:57:41,396 --> 00:57:45,942
We've decided to fight together
until the end,

951
00:57:46,025 --> 00:57:47,026
so, President Park,

952
00:57:47,860 --> 00:57:49,862
let's do this together.

953
00:57:51,281 --> 00:57:52,115
All right.

954
00:57:52,198 --> 00:57:54,450
But I'm doing this my way.

955
00:57:54,534 --> 00:57:57,120
I want you all to have my back,

956
00:57:57,203 --> 00:58:01,040
so no one can touch my sledgehammer.

957
00:58:01,708 --> 00:58:03,459
Let's protect True Value.

958
00:58:03,543 --> 00:58:04,669
Yes!

959
00:58:05,253 --> 00:58:07,797
-Let's protect True Value, everyone!
-Let's do it!

960
00:58:15,305 --> 00:58:16,139
Mr. Kim.

961
00:58:16,973 --> 00:58:18,099
Yes, sir.

962
00:58:19,058 --> 00:58:22,061
Do you know when you feel
the most despair in your life?

963
00:58:22,979 --> 00:58:27,108
When the ground collapses beneath you
just as you think you've made it.

964
00:58:29,277 --> 00:58:31,279
Park Hae-kang
is in that situation right now.

965
00:58:32,280 --> 00:58:34,699
He's all excited, thinking he's won.

966
00:58:41,748 --> 00:58:43,041
This smells nice.

967
00:58:44,792 --> 00:58:47,587
Just wait. I'll be there soon.

968
00:58:57,138 --> 00:58:58,514
Is that you, Hae-kang?

969
00:59:00,058 --> 00:59:01,643
Why are you here again?

970
00:59:08,858 --> 00:59:11,486
Mr. Park is a bit busy,

971
00:59:11,569 --> 00:59:13,404
so I came instead.

972
00:59:18,159 --> 00:59:20,286
Who are you?

973
00:59:21,037 --> 00:59:24,207
Mr. Park said he cares about you a lot,

974
00:59:24,290 --> 00:59:26,209
so I was curious.

975
00:59:32,632 --> 00:59:36,511
Mr. Park is going through a lot
because of you.

976
00:59:37,178 --> 00:59:39,347
You don't share a drop of blood,

977
00:59:39,430 --> 00:59:41,391
yet he's ruining his own life

978
00:59:42,350 --> 00:59:45,144
over so-called loyalty.

979
00:59:47,188 --> 00:59:48,523
He's always been

980
00:59:50,066 --> 00:59:52,610
foolishly loyal.

981
00:59:57,657 --> 00:59:58,825
Who…

982
00:59:59,742 --> 01:00:00,660
are you?

983
01:00:01,994 --> 01:00:05,456
I'm here to clean up the garbage
that he hasn't been able to get rid of.

984
01:00:06,624 --> 01:00:08,251
Garbage?

985
01:00:11,254 --> 01:00:12,463
It's foolish,

986
01:00:12,547 --> 01:00:15,550
clinging to a losing card until the end.

987
01:00:16,092 --> 01:00:17,593
My mom did that too.

988
01:00:18,219 --> 01:00:21,389
She stood her ground
against the demolition crew swinging bats

989
01:00:21,973 --> 01:00:25,059
just to protect a house
that was already falling apart.

990
01:00:25,852 --> 01:00:28,229
She got carried out, covered in blood,

991
01:00:28,896 --> 01:00:31,482
but the world was so quiet.

992
01:00:32,567 --> 01:00:33,818
That's when I realized

993
01:00:35,403 --> 01:00:37,488
that I shouldn't take away the bats.

994
01:00:37,572 --> 01:00:39,782
I should keep the ones wielding them

995
01:00:40,283 --> 01:00:42,910
beneath my feet.

996
01:00:44,787 --> 01:00:45,997
You're…

997
01:00:47,623 --> 01:00:49,125
really…

998
01:00:50,585 --> 01:00:51,502
pitiful.

999
01:01:00,553 --> 01:01:02,138
What did you just say?

1000
01:01:05,141 --> 01:01:08,269
You've piled up mountains of money,

1001
01:01:10,229 --> 01:01:11,522
but your heart

1002
01:01:12,774 --> 01:01:16,986
is still that of the little boy
at the demolition site,

1003
01:01:18,112 --> 01:01:20,990
trembling in fear.

1004
01:01:23,618 --> 01:01:25,787
You're still a pitiful boy

1005
01:01:26,704 --> 01:01:29,957
scattering poison everywhere

1006
01:01:31,250 --> 01:01:33,836
so you won't…

1007
01:01:37,131 --> 01:01:38,299
get beaten.

1008
01:01:40,593 --> 01:01:44,305
Those are pretty harsh words
coming from a dying man.

1009
01:01:46,307 --> 01:01:47,725
"Pitiful"?

1010
01:02:02,448 --> 01:02:05,785
That pitiful boy will give you a present.

1011
01:02:16,462 --> 01:02:18,548
PARK ****-MAN

1012
01:02:24,637 --> 01:02:28,891
You're really pitiful.

1013
01:02:29,392 --> 01:02:32,728
You're still a pitiful boy
scattering poison everywhere

1014
01:02:33,646 --> 01:02:36,190
so you won't…

1015
01:02:37,233 --> 01:02:38,276
get beaten.

1016
01:03:53,351 --> 01:03:54,685
Yong-man.

1017
01:03:55,895 --> 01:03:56,854
Yong-man.

1018
01:03:57,730 --> 01:03:59,065
I'm here.

1019
01:04:01,525 --> 01:04:02,401
Yong-man.

1020
01:04:03,653 --> 01:04:05,154
Yong-man, it's me.

1021
01:04:05,237 --> 01:04:06,155
Yong-man!

1022
01:04:16,540 --> 01:04:17,458
Someone…

1023
01:04:18,084 --> 01:04:19,043
Excuse me.

1024
01:04:21,045 --> 01:04:22,254
Anyone?

1025
01:04:28,970 --> 01:04:30,554
Please save Yong-man.

1026
01:04:31,681 --> 01:04:33,349
Please save him…

1027
01:04:36,310 --> 01:04:39,105
Please save Yong-man…

1028
01:04:42,566 --> 01:04:45,653
Someone, please save him…

1029
01:05:30,865 --> 01:05:32,366
CONDOLENCE BOX

1030
01:05:33,868 --> 01:05:34,869
What?

1031
01:05:37,371 --> 01:05:38,831
LEE CHUNG-WON

1032
01:06:30,841 --> 01:06:33,177
I was startled

1033
01:06:34,053 --> 01:06:35,638
when I heard the news.

1034
01:06:36,430 --> 01:06:37,765
I heard

1035
01:06:38,474 --> 01:06:41,227
he was like a father to you.

1036
01:06:42,645 --> 01:06:44,438
You must be devastated.

1037
01:06:49,151 --> 01:06:50,778
I happened to be there

1038
01:06:51,570 --> 01:06:54,031
in his final moments.

1039
01:06:56,408 --> 01:06:58,119
Why did you do it?

1040
01:06:59,120 --> 01:07:01,664
You should have been there for him

1041
01:07:01,747 --> 01:07:03,999
when he passed away.

1042
01:07:05,543 --> 01:07:07,253
But don't worry.

1043
01:07:08,671 --> 01:07:11,006
He didn't suffer when he passed.

1044
01:07:12,591 --> 01:07:13,425
You…

1045
01:07:17,429 --> 01:07:18,722
What did you do?

1046
01:07:22,601 --> 01:07:23,435
Huh?

1047
01:07:28,774 --> 01:07:30,317
Remember how I said

1048
01:07:30,901 --> 01:07:33,237
hangnails should be ripped off,
even if you bleed?

1049
01:07:34,613 --> 01:07:37,074
He seemed to be a hangnail

1050
01:07:37,158 --> 01:07:39,869
in your life.

1051
01:07:40,828 --> 01:07:44,123
So I ripped it off for you.

1052
01:07:45,374 --> 01:07:46,959
Don't you feel relieved now?

1053
01:07:52,756 --> 01:07:54,925
I offer my deepest…

1054
01:07:56,260 --> 01:07:57,761
condolences.

1055
01:08:32,171 --> 01:08:35,090
THE APARTMENT JOB

1056
01:08:59,198 --> 01:09:00,115
THE LATE PARK YONG-MAN

1057
01:09:00,199 --> 01:09:02,326
You have to win, no matter what it takes.

1058
01:09:02,409 --> 01:09:03,577
That's what you have to do.

1059
01:09:03,661 --> 01:09:06,580
I'll live my life
proving that you were right.

1060
01:09:06,664 --> 01:09:09,875
Cut the prices
of the Oman New Town units in half.

1061
01:09:09,959 --> 01:09:11,335
We will be reborn.

1062
01:09:11,418 --> 01:09:15,214
Shouldn't we scrape together
every last penny to save our company?

1063
01:09:15,297 --> 01:09:17,258
Please have mercy, sir!

1064
01:09:17,341 --> 01:09:19,677
Taegowon isn't just a tree farm, is it?

1065
01:09:19,760 --> 01:09:22,596
Whenever we took money out of the fund,
we delivered it to Taegowon.

1066
01:09:22,680 --> 01:09:24,807
Then our 17.8 billion should be there too.

1067
01:09:24,890 --> 01:09:26,016
Should we steal it back?

1068
01:09:26,100 --> 01:09:27,685
Yes. He values that more than his life.

1069
01:09:27,768 --> 01:09:30,312
They have such pretty nameplates
for every tree.

1070
01:09:30,396 --> 01:09:32,439
Do you have a death wish?

1071
01:09:32,523 --> 01:09:33,899
Should I try digging?

1072
01:09:33,983 --> 01:09:35,693
Change all the license plates.

1073
01:09:35,776 --> 01:09:38,028
Move everything,
and don't leave a speck of dirt behind.

1074
01:09:38,112 --> 01:09:41,240
But Taesan's warehouse will be too risky.

1075
01:09:41,323 --> 01:09:42,491
That one!

1076
01:09:42,574 --> 01:09:45,035
I know a place.
Somewhere no one can even imagine.

1077
01:09:45,119 --> 01:09:46,787
Are you ready? Run!

1078
01:09:48,789 --> 01:09:50,791
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

